{"kind":"report","text":"Ready for review at exact clean head d428ca97f31b758ec07b94796aa323528b3aac79 on task/mcp-repo-parameter. The repository is a call parameter defaulting to the adapter's working directory; a named repository is reached instead when given, and linked worktrees of one repository resolve to one workroom. A directory with no workroom, or one where the actor is not configured, fails that call and leaves the connection working. The resident service is read from the repository and used only when the genesis recorded with it matches, an address that stops answering is forgotten and looked up again, and the degraded local path is unchanged when none is reachable. Serving binds before it advertises, publishes the bound address, and withdraws it on exit unless a later service took it over. --server is accepted and ignored with a note on stderr so existing registrations keep working. Gates: go vet, go test, go test -race, and go build all pass; new tests cover repository selection, calls outside a workroom, service discovery and genesis refusal, rediscovery after a service moves, concurrent presence renewal, and serve publication and withdrawal. Verified by hand from a directory that is not a repository: the adapter stayed up, reported the absence, and answered for two named repositories including a linked worktree. Not done: the codex and Claude Code registrations still pass the retired --server and an absolute --repo, and the running service predates publication, so both want updating after merge.","body":{"branch":"task/mcp-repo-parameter","head":"d428ca97f31b758ec07b94796aa323528b3aac79","task":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b72ecf8b7aeaa66fe271ba1a200386eb37f1cca6"}}